 Pi can explain its own features and look up its docs. Ask it how to use or extend Pi.


 Explain in two sentences what a fixed-layout terminal is.


 A fixed-layout terminal is a terminal program whose window size, font, and panel arrangement are fixed at
 configuration time rather than dynamically reflowing with the window contents. This gives predictable screen geometry
 for scripts and TUIs, but at the cost of flexibility compared to resize-aware modern emulators.

